WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:10.707
In April 2023, Mr Guo, who runs a tech company in Fuzhou, got a WeChat video call from a friend.

2
00:00:11.057 --> 00:00:19.432
The friend said someone needed a 4.3 million yuan bid deposit, and asked to route it through Guo's company account.

3
00:00:19.782 --> 00:00:29.187
On screen it was the friend's face and the friend's voice. Without checking that any money had arrived, Guo sent 4.3 million.

4
00:00:29.537 --> 00:00:40.541
Then he phoned the friend, who said it never happened. Baotou police reported that scammers had used AI face-swapping to impersonate the friend.

5
00:00:40.891 --> 00:00:48.068
Guo said afterwards: I saw the face and heard the voice on the video, so I let my guard down.

6
00:00:48.867 --> 00:00:53.885
This is C5: safety, privacy and scams.

7
00:00:54.235 --> 00:01:01.636
You'll learn how to guard against face-swap and voice-clone scams, and what not to give an AI.

8
00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:13.445
AI can synthesise someone's face and voice from their photos, videos and recordings. This is called deep synthesis, or face-swapping and voice cloning.

9
00:01:13.795 --> 00:01:27.365
The raw material scammers need is your face and your voice. Financial regulators warn they pose as customer service, recruiters or dates to collect your voice and facial information.

10
00:01:27.715 --> 00:01:35.517
The US consumer protection agency warns that a short audio clip is enough to clone a family member's voice.

11
00:01:35.867 --> 00:01:42.472
So remember: seeing isn't always believing, and neither is hearing.

12
00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:46.662
These scams usually share a few signs.

13
00:01:47.012 --> 00:01:53.383
One: they want money, urgently. There's been an accident; a deposit is needed now.

14
00:01:53.733 --> 00:02:00.513
Two: one channel only. Only on this video call, only on this number.

15
00:02:00.863 --> 00:02:04.845
Three: secrecy. Don't tell Mum and Dad.

16
00:02:05.195 --> 00:02:11.182
Four: payment that's hard to recover, like wire transfers or gift cards.

17
00:02:11.532 --> 00:02:15.904
When you see these signs, stop. Don't rush to transfer money.

18
00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:22.115
So what do you do? Don't rely on your eyes or ears. Rely on a routine.

19
00:02:22.465 --> 00:02:29.855
Whenever money is involved, hang up and call back on the number already saved in your own phone. Ask the person directly.

20
00:02:30.455 --> 00:02:41.628
China's Ministry of Public Security warns: before any transfer, verify through the original contact details or several channels, never a single video call.

21
00:02:41.978 --> 00:02:49.159
You can also agree a code word that only your family knows. If the caller can't say it, be careful.

22
00:02:49.509 --> 00:02:59.297
If in doubt, call 96110, the police anti-fraud warning and advice line, for advice or to report.

23
00:03:00.068 --> 00:03:08.832
Now, our own use of AI. China's national security authorities warn that AI tools can collect and store what you type in.

24
00:03:09.182 --> 00:03:20.206
So don't give an AI your ID number, bank card number, passwords or verification codes, and don't casually upload photos or recordings of yourself and your family.

25
00:03:20.556 --> 00:03:28.742
For medical records, other people's private details or work files, remove names and describe the situation, or don't paste the original at all.

26
00:03:29.092 --> 00:03:33.866
In short: treat anything you give an AI as something others might see.

27
00:03:34.635 --> 00:03:45.240
One more new rule: since 1 September 2025, AI-generated text, images, audio and video must carry a label.

28
00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:55.972
An 'AI-generated' label means it's synthetic. But no label doesn't mean it's real; scammers don't label their fakes.

29
00:03:56.322 --> 00:04:01.727
If you make images or videos with AI, label them when you post them.

30
00:04:02.502 --> 00:04:17.250
Remember: three red lines, one phone call. Money, health, personal information: verify first; hang up and call back on your saved number; if in doubt, call 96110.

31
00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:24.779
Quick exercise: agree a family code word today, and practise hanging up and calling back.

32
00:04:25.129 --> 00:04:30.125
Next time, C6: fairness, ethics and work.
